{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Ozen","id":"321508500138360843","is_bot":0,"username":"ozenannwn"},"author_id":"321508500138360843","channel_id":"736679166262509618","content":"Went looking for a gender-neutral term for lord/lady and found this:\n\nlord < ME lavord < OE hlafweard = hlaf + weard (loaf - keeper) is the one who keeps your loaf of bread, and grants you some to eat once a day. Traditionally a man, but not a gendered word.\n\nlady < ME ladiye < OE hlafdige = hlaf + dige (loaf - kneader) is the one who actually makes that loaf of bread and presumably hands it to the loaf-keeper for safekeeping. Again not gendered in any linguistic sense.","created_at":"2020-08-17T21:45:58.588000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"745035723547344936","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
